1
00:00:00,550 --> 00:00:02,425
Two instruction manuals.

2
00:00:02,425 --> 00:00:06,800
One thousand six hundred and twenty-three scanned pages.

3
00:00:06,800 --> 00:00:09,768
And not a single searchable character.

4
00:00:09,768 --> 00:00:13,362
Finding one safety rule could take an evening.

5
00:00:13,362 --> 00:00:15,784
This is the problem PDF Q and A

6
00:00:15,784 --> 00:00:17,190
was built to kill.

7
00:00:19,050 --> 00:00:20,549
This is PDF Q and A.

8
00:00:20,549 --> 00:00:23,921
Drop in any PDF, even a thousand-page scanned

9
00:00:23,921 --> 00:00:27,593
manual, and it reads every page, saves everything

10
00:00:27,593 --> 00:00:31,190
into a database, and answers your questions with

11
00:00:31,190 --> 00:00:32,838
the exact page number.

12
00:00:32,838 --> 00:00:33,513
No cloud.

13
00:00:33,513 --> 00:00:34,712
No subscription.

14
00:00:34,712 --> 00:00:36,810
It runs on your own machine.

15
00:00:38,550 --> 00:00:41,440
Uploading is drag and drop, up to twenty

16
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:42,452
files at once.

17
00:00:42,452 --> 00:00:45,631
Scanned pages are read locally by Rapid OCR,

18
00:00:45,631 --> 00:00:48,233
and you watch every page land in the

19
00:00:48,233 --> 00:00:49,244
database live:

20
00:00:49,244 --> 00:00:52,135
page number, percentage, time remaining.

21
00:00:52,135 --> 00:00:54,230
Nothing leaves your computer.

22
00:00:56,050 --> 00:00:56,575
Now ask.

23
00:00:56,575 --> 00:00:59,069
The answer comes back with its source:

24
00:00:59,069 --> 00:01:01,497
the file name, the page number, and a

25
00:01:01,497 --> 00:01:02,285
match score.

26
00:01:02,285 --> 00:01:04,845
Open the sources and you are looking at

27
00:01:04,845 --> 00:01:07,273
the exact passage the database found.

28
00:01:07,273 --> 00:01:09,570
You can verify everything yourself.

29
00:01:11,050 --> 00:01:12,630
Here is the pipeline.

30
00:01:12,630 --> 00:01:15,565
The browser talks to an Express server.

31
00:01:15,565 --> 00:01:18,801
A Python worker extracts text with PyMuPDF;

32
00:01:18,801 --> 00:01:21,435
scanned pages go through Rapid OCR.

33
00:01:21,435 --> 00:01:24,972
Prisma writes every page and chunk into SQLite,

34
00:01:24,972 --> 00:01:27,154
with an FTS5 full-text index.

35
00:01:27,154 --> 00:01:30,240
A question runs a BM25 search first, then

36
00:01:30,240 --> 00:01:33,250
builds the answer from the top passages.

37
00:01:35,050 --> 00:01:36,496
Then the AI chain.

38
00:01:36,496 --> 00:01:40,352
Ollama runs first, entirely on your own machine.

39
00:01:40,352 --> 00:01:43,967
Then GLM, NVIDIA NIM, OpenRouter, and Gemini.

40
00:01:43,967 --> 00:01:47,502
If one provider fails, the next one answers.

41
00:01:47,502 --> 00:01:50,876
And if every provider fails, you still get

42
00:01:50,876 --> 00:01:52,482
the database answer.

43
00:01:52,482 --> 00:01:54,330
The system never stops.

44
00:01:56,050 --> 00:01:59,701
Libraries and models, exactly as shipped.

45
00:01:59,701 --> 00:02:01,839
Node twenty and Express.

46
00:02:01,839 --> 00:02:05,045
Prisma seven with the libSQL driver.

47
00:02:05,045 --> 00:02:08,874
SQLite with an FTS5 index and BM25 ranking.

48
00:02:08,874 --> 00:02:11,368
PyMuPDF for text and layout.

49
00:02:11,368 --> 00:02:13,683
Rapid OCR on ONNX Runtime.

50
00:02:13,683 --> 00:02:18,136
Ollama runs Qwen two point five, seven B, locally.

51
00:02:18,136 --> 00:02:21,609
The cloud chain is GLM four point seven

52
00:02:21,609 --> 00:02:27,131
Flash, NVIDIA Nemotron three point five Lightning, OpenRouter,

53
00:02:27,131 --> 00:02:29,090
and Gemini Flash Lite.

54
00:02:30,550 --> 00:02:33,028
And this film was built the same way.

55
00:02:33,028 --> 00:02:36,176
Brag supplied the storyboard, the music and the

56
00:02:36,176 --> 00:02:37,114
sound effects.

57
00:02:37,114 --> 00:02:40,463
Cinematic Skill drove the camera and the captions.

58
00:02:40,463 --> 00:02:43,276
Voice Studio shaped the voice and the mix.

59
00:02:43,276 --> 00:02:46,558
Omni Voice guided the multilingual speech design.

60
00:02:46,558 --> 00:02:49,840
And Playwright MCP took every real screenshot you

61
00:02:49,840 --> 00:02:50,510
have seen.

62
00:02:52,050 --> 00:02:53,733
Your data stays yours.

63
00:02:53,733 --> 00:02:56,563
View any page, export to text, CSV or

64
00:02:56,563 --> 00:02:59,088
JSON, delete with a confirmation.

65
00:02:59,088 --> 00:03:01,459
The whole app works on a phone.

66
00:03:01,459 --> 00:03:05,054
And a complete Docker plus EC2 deployment guide

67
00:03:05,054 --> 00:03:06,890
ships in the repository.

68
00:03:08,550 --> 00:03:09,374
Setup is one command.

69
00:03:09,374 --> 00:03:10,119
Run is one command.

70
00:03:10,119 --> 00:03:11,060
Then drop a PDF and ask.

71
00:03:11,060 --> 00:03:12,707
The full guide, the Word documents and the

72
00:03:12,707 --> 00:03:13,766
code are in the repository.

73
00:03:13,766 --> 00:03:14,550
Thanks for watching.

